Cloud model — the same file text and path leave this machine.                                       
                                                                                                    
Destination: https://api.anthropic.com (backend "work")                                             
Credential: read from $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY at request time                                            
Transport: the curl program on this system                                                          
                                                                                                    
Once the text is sent, yew cannot recall it, cannot delete it, and does not know how long it is kept
 or who can read it. That is between you and Anthropic, under their terms — which yew neither contro
ls nor recites here, because they change and this text does not.                                    
                                                                                                    
yew scans every request for secrets first. If it finds one, the request is BLOCKED and names the mat
ching line. It does not scrub and send: a scrubber that is 99% right leaks on the hundredth file.   
                                                                                                    
Type the word 'send' to confirm you want file contents sent to api.anthropic.com, or press Esc to ca
ncel:                                                                                               
:                                                                                                   
